<title>USA: USDA eyes grain reserve, loan extension - Glickman.</title>
<headline>USDA eyes grain reserve, loan extension - Glickman.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>There is &quot;no legislative proposal yet,&quot; Agriculture Secretary Dan Glickman said Thursday, but the department continues to look at a grain reserve and loan extensions as ways to aid farmers.</p>
<p>&quot;We haven't priced this out,&quot; Glickman told reporters.</p>
<p>He also said fundamental change of the &quot;Freedom to Farm&quot; law was unlikely. It ended the long-term Farmer Owned Reserve.</p>
<p>Glickman said changes in USDA farm lending rules and in crop insurance also were being explored.</p>
</text>
